From 7ceb647f753f6417fc1a8d7a791a846afdbe2f4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 08:18:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: restrict BRF kcov instrumentation to softirq context

A fuzz run on the BRF MPTCP harness hit:

  WARNING: kernel/kcov.c:971 at kcov_remote_start_prealloc
   mptcp_incoming_options       net/mptcp/options.c:1195
   tcp_data_queue / tcp_rcv_established / tcp_v6_do_rcv
   sk_backlog_rcv / __release_sock / release_sock
   __mptcp_push_pending / mptcp_sendmsg / __sys_sendto

kcov_remote_start() warns when it is called in process context
from a task that already has kcov enabled (the WARN_ON at
kernel/kcov.c:971).

The BRF kcov wraps -- the MP_JOIN validity gates from "mptcp:
instrument MP_JOIN validity gates with kcov" and the option
parser from "mptcp: extend kcov instrumentation to the option
parser" -- assumed their call sites run only in softirq.  That
holds for the inbound-packet softirq path, but the same MPTCP RX
code also runs in process context: release_sock() drains the
socket backlog inline, in the context of whatever syscall held
and dropped the socket lock (here sendto()).  The syz-executor
task has kcov enabled, so kcov_remote_start_prealloc() warns,
and syzkaller treats the WARNING as a crash.

Guard BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START / _STOP with in_serving_softirq() so
the kcov_remote section is entered only in genuine softirq
context.  In process context the calling task's own per-task
kcov already records this code, so the remote section was never
needed there -- the guard removes the warning and loses no
coverage.  Because the guard lives in the shared macros it also
covers the three MP_JOIN gates, which have the same latent
exposure on the backlog path.

start and stop evaluate in_serving_softirq() over the same
synchronous region, so they stay balanced.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Signed-off-by: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
---
 net/mptcp/protocol.h | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/protocol.h b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
index 8367ea768375e..409c960c80374 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.h
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
@@ -1449,6 +1449,15 @@ static inline void mptcp_join_cookie_init(void) {}
  * subflows of the msk so concurrent gates race.  See the
  * comment on kcov_coverage_area in struct mptcp_sock and the
  * design doc kernel_base_management.md (sibling brf repo).
+ *
+ * Fires only in softirq context.  kcov_remote_start() WARNs
+ * (kernel/kcov.c) when called in process context from a task
+ * that already has kcov enabled -- and the wrapped MPTCP RX
+ * paths also run in process context, draining the socket
+ * backlog from release_sock() inside a syscall.  There the
+ * calling task's own per-task kcov already records this code,
+ * so the remote section is both unnecessary and unsafe;
+ * in_serving_softirq() gates it.
  */
 #define BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(__msk)					\
 	do {								\
@@ -1457,7 +1466,8 @@ static inline void mptcp_join_cookie_init(void) {}
 		if (!__m)						\
 			break;						\
 		__h = READ_ONCE(__m->kcov_remote_handle);		\
-		if (__h && __m->kcov_coverage_area)			\
+		if (__h && __m->kcov_coverage_area &&			\
+		    in_serving_softirq())				\
 			kcov_remote_start_prealloc(__h,			\
 				__m->kcov_coverage_area,		\
 				__m->kcov_area_size);			\
@@ -1466,7 +1476,8 @@ static inline void mptcp_join_cookie_init(void) {}
 	do {								\
 		struct mptcp_sock *__m = (__msk);			\
 		if (__m && READ_ONCE(__m->kcov_remote_handle) &&	\
-		    __m->kcov_coverage_area)				\
+		    __m->kcov_coverage_area &&				\
+		    in_serving_softirq())				\
 			kcov_remote_stop_prealloc();			\
 	} while (0)
 #else

